1
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:44,293
"Stay calm."

2
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:47,463
Do that, nothing can go wrong.
Got it?

3
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:49,382
Yeah, we got it.

4
00:00:54,762 --> 00:00:56,097
Hi, good to see you again.

5
00:00:56,222 --> 00:01:00,017
Uh, yes, that time of the year.
I have to get my shoes resoled.

6
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:02,186
- Uh, put. Put.
- Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

7
00:01:03,479 --> 00:01:06,566
Right there.
Got just a... a hole there.

8
00:01:15,491 --> 00:01:17,785
Everybody, get down!
This is a robbery!

9
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:21,372
Get out from behind the counter.
Get out here! Now!

10
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:24,125
Get down!
Down!

11
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:27,003
Get down!
Get down on the ground!

12
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:29,630
Nobody do anything stupid!

13
00:01:30,172 --> 00:01:31,215
Cameras. Move.

14
00:01:31,465 --> 00:01:34,427
I wanna cell phones kicked into
the center of the room right now.

15
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:36,304
Let's see 'em!

16
00:01:40,558 --> 00:01:42,018
- Name.
- Still Jane.

17
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:50,776
Thank you.

18
00:01:52,194 --> 00:01:53,237
And, uh...

19
00:01:53,654 --> 00:01:54,697
how long do you think
that'll be?

20
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:56,490
We'll see.

21
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:58,492
Okay.

22
00:01:59,368 --> 00:02:00,411
Good to see you, too.

23
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:07,710
Everybody's gonna go home
to their families

24
00:02:07,835 --> 00:02:09,337
if they don't do
anything stupid.

25
00:02:10,796 --> 00:02:12,298
Who here can open the vault?

26
00:02:13,215 --> 00:02:14,258
I can. I can.

27
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:16,636
Get up! Get in the back!

28
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:19,347
Get the bags.

29
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:31,776
Go!

30
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:37,948
Open it.

31
00:02:42,828 --> 00:02:43,954
Hey. Kill it.

32
00:02:59,428 --> 00:03:00,763
Here. Fill it.

33
00:03:23,285 --> 00:03:24,328
Fill it.

34
00:03:37,633 --> 00:03:38,676
What's taking him so long?

35
00:03:47,309 --> 00:03:48,352
We don't need these.

36
00:03:51,230 --> 00:03:52,273
Count to a hundred.

37
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,775
One

38
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:56,110
two

39
00:03:56,652 --> 00:03:57,695
three...

40
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:03,492
What the hell was that?

41
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:20,176
Let's go!

42
00:04:22,845 --> 00:04:23,888
Back up, come on.

43
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,490
"Hey, you idiot! You hit my car!"

44
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:45,367
There's a cop.

45
00:04:59,131 --> 00:05:01,550
I think you need a little lie-down.
Just have a little rest here.

46
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:03,344
- I think I might faint.
- Okay. There we go.

47
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:04,553
Just put your head down there.

48
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:18,982
Okay. Thanks.

49
00:05:20,359 --> 00:05:22,361
Three men hit the vault
in the back for a million in cash.

50
00:05:22,694 --> 00:05:24,112
They shot killed
an assistant manager.

51
00:05:24,446 --> 00:05:25,489
Any witnesses?

52
00:05:25,656 --> 00:05:27,199
Lots, but they're not much help.

53
00:05:27,449 --> 00:05:28,492
The robbers were wearing masks.

54
00:05:28,826 --> 00:05:30,619
{\an8}They also blacked out
the cameras with spray paint

55
00:05:30,828 --> 00:05:31,870
{\an8}but I'm pulling the footage.

56
00:05:32,162 --> 00:05:33,789
- Where's Jane?
- Inside.

57
00:05:37,251 --> 00:05:39,169
- Is that a friend of the victim?
- Fiancée.

58
00:05:39,628 --> 00:05:40,879
Works in the bank.

59
00:05:52,891 --> 00:05:53,934
{\an8}Hey.

60
00:05:56,311 --> 00:05:57,354
Nice shoes.

61
00:05:58,605 --> 00:06:01,108
{\an8}Uh, yes, uh, loaners.

62
00:06:02,067 --> 00:06:03,235
{\an8}Mine are in getting repaired.

63
00:06:04,152 --> 00:06:05,195
How long is that gonna take?

64
00:06:05,988 --> 00:06:07,447
{\an8}We'll see. The, uh...

65
00:06:08,657 --> 00:06:09,700
cobbler fainted.

66
00:06:19,668 --> 00:06:20,711
{\an8}Are you coming?

67
00:06:21,169 --> 00:06:22,212
{\an8}Meh.

68
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,007
{\an8}It's a little cramped in there.

69
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,372
{\an8}No expended casings in here.
Any outside?

70
00:06:57,956 --> 00:06:59,583
Found 2. Both 9 millimeter.

71
00:07:00,125 --> 00:07:02,085
Witnesses say six shots
were fired outside

72
00:07:02,294 --> 00:07:04,004
so one of the shooters
must've been using a revolver.

73
00:07:04,338 --> 00:07:07,049
{\an8}Let me know what the M.E. says
when he pulls the slug from the victim.

74
00:07:07,424 --> 00:07:08,926
{\an8}- You got anything?
- Maybe.

75
00:07:09,843 --> 00:07:11,261
{\an8}I just spoke
with a SAC P.D. detective

76
00:07:11,386 --> 00:07:12,512
who thinks
this robbery's connected

77
00:07:12,638 --> 00:07:14,640
with three others committed
in the past six months.

78
00:07:14,765 --> 00:07:16,892
In all of them, two, sometimes
three masked men

79
00:07:17,059 --> 00:07:19,436
{\an8}took out the security cameras,
passed up the teller drawers

80
00:07:19,686 --> 00:07:21,480
{\an8}and went straight for the vault,
just like these guys.

81
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:23,106
How many victims
in the other robberies?

82
00:07:23,357 --> 00:07:24,650
None. He's the first.

83
00:07:32,616 --> 00:07:34,159
{\an8}Did SAC P.D. finish
their search of the bank?

84
00:07:34,368 --> 00:07:35,994
Almost. Nothing so far.

85
00:07:36,703 --> 00:07:38,121
Okay. Here's how
we're gonna run this.

86
00:07:38,246 --> 00:07:39,581
You coordinate the witness interviews

87
00:07:39,706 --> 00:07:42,292
and tell Rigsby to pull the case files
from the other robberies.

88
00:07:42,501 --> 00:07:44,419
- I wanna know if this is the same guys.
- All right.

89
00:07:45,545 --> 00:07:47,005
- This is Lisbon.
- Cho.

90
00:07:47,798 --> 00:07:49,841
Was the safe deposit vault
open when you got here?

91
00:07:50,425 --> 00:07:51,468
Yeah. Why?

92
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:53,053
Just curious.

93
00:07:53,178 --> 00:07:54,596
Yes, sir.
I will be right there.

94
00:07:55,806 --> 00:07:56,932
That was Bertram.
I gotta go.

95
00:07:59,309 --> 00:08:01,561
Bank robberies belong
to the FBI.

96
00:08:02,062 --> 00:08:03,105
This case is ours.

97
00:08:03,230 --> 00:08:04,272
And tell me, why does the CBI

98
00:08:04,398 --> 00:08:06,274
continue to encroach
on our jurisdiction?

99
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,567
We were on site first.

100
00:08:07,693 --> 00:08:09,277
It's not our fault
if you're late off the mark.

101
00:08:09,695 --> 00:08:11,989
Agent Lisbon, Agent Mancini
has a valid point

102
00:08:12,114 --> 00:08:13,615
- regarding jurisdiction.
- Thank you.

103
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:15,826
Sir, the crime my team and I
are investigating

104
00:08:15,951 --> 00:08:17,285
is a crime of murder.

105
00:08:17,619 --> 00:08:19,246
A murder committed
during a bank robbery.

106
00:08:19,371 --> 00:08:22,207
The murder supersedes
the crime of armed robbery.

107
00:08:22,332 --> 00:08:24,334
So our investigation
takes priority.

108
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:26,294
You're more than welcome
to investigate

109
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:27,963
after we close the murder.

110
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:29,798
- Assuming you do.
- You know what they say

111
00:08:29,923 --> 00:08:31,591
- about assuming things. It makes--
- I know exactly what--

112
00:08:31,717 --> 00:08:33,427
All right. That's enough.

113
00:08:37,472 --> 00:08:39,975
Agent Mancini, Agent Lisbon
and her team will take point

114
00:08:40,142 --> 00:08:41,393
in the murder investigation.

115
00:08:41,518 --> 00:08:44,855
In the meantime, you will have
full access to all case files.

116
00:08:45,522 --> 00:08:46,565
Agreed?

117
00:08:51,286 --> 00:08:52,329
Hey.

118
00:08:52,746 --> 00:08:55,332
- We have a personal problem?
- Personal problem?

119
00:08:55,623 --> 00:08:56,833
You act like you don't like me

120
00:08:57,083 --> 00:08:58,460
like I killed your pet tortoise
or something.

121
00:08:58,752 --> 00:09:00,003
What, are we in high school?

122
00:09:00,170 --> 00:09:03,715
You lost the most important witness
we've ever had in the Red John case

123
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,425
and now you wonder why
I won't make nice?

124
00:09:05,550 --> 00:09:08,386
I didn't lose Lorelei Martins and I want her
back just as badly as you do.

125
00:09:08,595 --> 00:09:09,763
And generally speaking

126
00:09:09,929 --> 00:09:11,181
when people act like
they don't like me

127
00:09:11,348 --> 00:09:12,682
it's because they really do.

128
00:09:13,016 --> 00:09:15,352
- They just don't wanna admit it.
- Yeah. No.

129
00:09:15,894 --> 00:09:16,936
I don't like you.

130
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,231
You'll have the case files
by the end of the day.

131
00:09:20,774 --> 00:09:22,525
Listen, there's this poker game
we got going on.

132
00:09:22,650 --> 00:09:24,361
It's a friendly game,
mostly law enforcement

133
00:09:24,486 --> 00:09:26,071
State Department, FBI.
You want in?

134
00:09:26,488 --> 00:09:27,739
Maybe. When?

135
00:09:28,239 --> 00:09:29,282
I'll call you with the details.

136
00:09:30,033 --> 00:09:31,701
Good luck with the case.
Hope you find your man.

137
00:09:32,077 --> 00:09:33,119
All right.

138
00:09:34,412 --> 00:09:36,373
You boys leave tonight.
Don't come back.

139
00:09:36,664 --> 00:09:38,708
I don't wanna see you again.
Understood?

140
00:09:52,972 --> 00:09:54,933
Well, that was a complete
waste of time.

141
00:09:55,475 --> 00:09:58,019
Not one security camera near
SAC Federal caught the robbery.

142
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:00,939
- Thanks.
- Sure. What's all this?

143
00:10:01,606 --> 00:10:03,233
Case files and footage
from the other robberies.

144
00:10:03,733 --> 00:10:04,776
Check this out.

145
00:10:04,943 --> 00:10:07,153
The SAC Fed job
was by far the largest haul--

146
00:10:07,529 --> 00:10:09,155
more than double
any of the other robberies.

147
00:10:09,447 --> 00:10:11,366
- They're getting ambitious.
- Not they. He.

148
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:14,411
Now in each one of the robberies,
there's maybe 30 seconds of footage

149
00:10:14,577 --> 00:10:15,620
before the cameras were blacked out.

150
00:10:15,870 --> 00:10:17,914
That was enough to analyze
the suspects' height, weight

151
00:10:18,039 --> 00:10:19,666
build, and skin color, so I did.

152
00:10:20,125 --> 00:10:21,167
And guess what.

153
00:10:21,334 --> 00:10:23,795
Only one of the robbers
was involved in all four crimes.

154
00:10:25,088 --> 00:10:26,131
That's him.

155
00:10:26,756 --> 00:10:28,925
So the other robbers--
they were work for hire?

156
00:10:29,092 --> 00:10:30,927
Exactly. They do one job
and then they disappear.

157
00:10:31,052 --> 00:10:32,887
But if we can find this guy
we find them all.

158
00:10:33,263 --> 00:10:34,305
He's the key.

159
00:10:34,431 --> 00:10:35,890
Do you remember anything
about the men who did this?

160
00:10:36,015 --> 00:10:37,183
No. Not a thing.

161
00:10:37,767 --> 00:10:39,561
You know Ernie and I were up
for the same promotion?

162
00:10:40,061 --> 00:10:41,354
I was mad when I didn't get it.

163
00:10:42,147 --> 00:10:43,189
But not now.

164
00:10:44,107 --> 00:10:45,316
That could've been me
in there.

165
00:10:45,608 --> 00:10:48,486
Ernie was a good man.

166
00:10:49,112 --> 00:10:50,780
He didn't deserve this.

167
00:10:51,406 --> 00:10:52,699
What were you doing
during the robbery?

168
00:10:53,283 --> 00:10:54,451
What they told me to.

169
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:57,704
I am not trying to get shot
over this job.

170
00:10:58,413 --> 00:11:00,832
Ernie must've done something wrong.
Poor fool.

171
00:11:01,166 --> 00:11:03,042
And that's when the robbers
ordered you to the ground?

172
00:11:03,668 --> 00:11:05,295
Yeah. He stuck a gun
right in my face.

173
00:11:05,962 --> 00:11:08,423
I was gonna grab it
and take those guys down

174
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:10,592
but I just had back surgery

175
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:14,345
so I didn't wanna risk
the loss of innocent lives.

176
00:11:15,013 --> 00:11:16,389
After that, one of the robbers

177
00:11:16,598 --> 00:11:19,517
took assistant manager
Ernie Wright into the vault.

178
00:11:20,477 --> 00:11:22,896
I think so. I don't really know.
I was in the back.

179
00:11:23,188 --> 00:11:24,230
During the robbery?

180
00:11:24,772 --> 00:11:27,233
In the men's room.
Is this really necessary?

181
00:11:27,567 --> 00:11:28,610
- I've already been through--
- You were in the men's room

182
00:11:28,735 --> 00:11:29,777
the whole time?

183
00:11:29,903 --> 00:11:30,945
Yes.

184
00:11:31,237 --> 00:11:34,908
I was, uh, washing up
when I heard the gunshot.

185
00:11:35,158 --> 00:11:37,202
Of course, I didn't know it was
a gunshot at the time.

186
00:11:37,994 --> 00:11:41,164
It wasn't until I stepped into the hall
that I heard the screaming.

187
00:11:41,331 --> 00:11:42,415
Was anyone back there
with you?

188
00:11:42,707 --> 00:11:43,750
Not that I saw.

189
00:11:44,417 --> 00:11:46,085
Ernie and I had lunch plans.

190
00:11:47,212 --> 00:11:48,421
We were just about to leave

191
00:11:48,546 --> 00:11:51,174
when I went into the back
to use the restroom.

192
00:11:51,966 --> 00:11:53,927
Yes, we saw as much
on the security footage.

193
00:11:54,969 --> 00:11:57,263
We also saw your manager,
Armin Gagnon

194
00:11:57,388 --> 00:11:59,390
heading into the men's room
just behind you.

195
00:11:59,807 --> 00:12:01,643
- Do you remember seeing him?
- No.

196
00:12:02,936 --> 00:12:04,896
Not until after I heard the shot.

197
00:12:05,688 --> 00:12:08,399
I opened the door,
and Armin was standing there.

198
00:12:09,567 --> 00:12:11,861
Then I heard the robbers shouting,
so I closed the door

199
00:12:12,153 --> 00:12:14,989
and I-I hid in the stall
until they left.

200
00:12:15,448 --> 00:12:17,492
Mr. Gagnon was in the hallway?

201
00:12:18,368 --> 00:12:19,911
- Here?
- Yes.

202
00:12:20,870 --> 00:12:21,913
Why?

203
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:24,374
Just trying to get the facts
straight, ma'am.

204
00:12:24,832 --> 00:12:26,668
Was Ernie the type to fight back?

205
00:12:27,669 --> 00:12:28,711
No.

206
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:31,089
Ernie was a big Teddy bear.

207
00:12:32,465 --> 00:12:35,134
He'd never fight unless it was
to protect someone he loved.

208
00:12:41,891 --> 00:12:42,934
Hey. How's it going?

209
00:12:43,351 --> 00:12:45,311
- I think I got it.
- Okay. Lay it on me.

210
00:12:45,645 --> 00:12:46,688
This ringleader--

211
00:12:46,938 --> 00:12:48,815
he had to have planned
the robberies, right?

212
00:12:49,107 --> 00:12:50,149
Right.

213
00:12:50,275 --> 00:12:52,235
Which means he probably
visited each of the banks

214
00:12:52,402 --> 00:12:53,444
before he robbed them.

215
00:12:53,570 --> 00:12:55,488
On camera and without a mask, yeah.

216
00:12:55,613 --> 00:12:58,950
So we run all the security footage
through facial recognition software

217
00:12:59,075 --> 00:13:01,703
and when we find the man that visited
all four banks before the robberies

218
00:13:02,078 --> 00:13:03,746
- we find our ringleader.
- Great idea.

219
00:13:03,997 --> 00:13:07,333
It's an idea.
I don't know if I'd call it great.

220
00:13:07,584 --> 00:13:09,043
Ah, he's just jealous.

221
00:13:10,878 --> 00:13:13,131
- What are you wearing?
- Oh, these things?

222
00:13:13,965 --> 00:13:15,717
Ah, they're loaners.

223
00:13:16,634 --> 00:13:17,677
How about this?

224
00:13:18,094 --> 00:13:19,804
Whoever figures out
the bank robber's name first

225
00:13:19,929 --> 00:13:21,389
wins lunch for a week.

226
00:13:21,848 --> 00:13:23,808
Yeah, that usually
doesn't end well for us.

227
00:13:24,851 --> 00:13:26,811
What do you say, Grace?
You feeling lucky?

228
00:13:28,062 --> 00:13:29,105
You're on.

229
00:13:30,481 --> 00:13:31,524
Yeah.

230
00:13:35,486 --> 00:13:36,529
"It was closed."

231
00:13:37,071 --> 00:13:38,114
You're certain?

232
00:13:38,656 --> 00:13:39,866
Must've been closed.

233
00:13:40,617 --> 00:13:42,493
The safe deposit vault
is always closed.

234
00:13:45,788 --> 00:13:47,874
- I think it was closed.
- Yeah.

235
00:13:49,542 --> 00:13:50,710
I want you to close your eyes.

236
00:13:52,170 --> 00:13:54,088
Hey, we're grown-ups.
Come on.

237
00:13:56,132 --> 00:13:59,093
Now put your mental self
back in this very spot

238
00:13:59,594 --> 00:14:01,512
in that very moment.

239
00:14:02,597 --> 00:14:04,891
I want you to hear the sound
that your shoes made

240
00:14:05,391 --> 00:14:06,434
on this marble floor.

241
00:14:07,477 --> 00:14:09,187
Now without opening your eyes

242
00:14:10,021 --> 00:14:12,565
I want you to picture the door
as you pass by.

243
00:14:13,983 --> 00:14:15,026
Can you do that?

244
00:14:15,735 --> 00:14:17,195
Can you see the door?

245
00:14:17,904 --> 00:14:19,405
- Yes.
- And?

246
00:14:20,948 --> 00:14:21,991
It was open.

247
00:14:23,868 --> 00:14:26,245
Which means someone

248
00:14:26,913 --> 00:14:29,791
went inside the safe deposit
vault during the robbery.

249
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,876
Mostly likely a robber

250
00:14:32,001 --> 00:14:34,003
trying to take something
from a deposit box.

251
00:14:34,128 --> 00:14:35,505
Oh, my. What if they did?

252
00:14:36,005 --> 00:14:37,131
Let's find out, shall we?

253
00:14:37,548 --> 00:14:39,008
- That's impossible.
- It is?

254
00:14:39,425 --> 00:14:41,844
The safe deposit boxes
are legal property

255
00:14:41,969 --> 00:14:43,388
of the individuals who rent them.

256
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,807
We don't even have keys.
Only the owners do.

257
00:14:45,973 --> 00:14:47,016
Only the owners do.

258
00:14:48,017 --> 00:14:49,852
You wouldn't happen to have a list
of those names, would you?

259
00:14:51,938 --> 00:14:52,980
We got a match.

260
00:14:53,272 --> 00:14:54,482
Oh, good morning to you, too.

261
00:14:54,816 --> 00:14:56,943
The suspect visited
Pacific Bank of Modesto

262
00:14:57,193 --> 00:14:59,570
and Fresno Savings and Loan
a week before each was robbed.

263
00:14:59,696 --> 00:15:01,322
He comes in, cases the place,
then leaves

264
00:15:01,447 --> 00:15:03,282
without making a transaction.
I think we found our guy.

265
00:15:03,991 --> 00:15:06,452
- His name anyway.
- Well, congratulations.

266
00:15:07,704 --> 00:15:08,746
Me, too.

267
00:15:09,122 --> 00:15:10,581
You did? When?

268
00:15:10,915 --> 00:15:12,166
When did you figure it out?

269
00:15:12,959 --> 00:15:14,001
About an hour ago.

270
00:15:14,252 --> 00:15:15,670
Ah, well, there you have it.

271
00:15:15,878 --> 00:15:19,632
I figured it out two hours ago
so it looks like I win the bet.

272
00:15:21,175 --> 00:15:22,218
Okay, what's his name?

273
00:15:22,343 --> 00:15:24,721
Oh, I'm not gonna fall
for that old trick, Grace.

274
00:15:25,722 --> 00:15:28,349
Write it down on a piece of paper
so I know that you're not lying.

275
00:15:41,279 --> 00:15:43,197
John Hutten.

276
00:15:45,408 --> 00:15:46,451
How did you do that?

277
00:15:46,868 --> 00:15:49,495
How did I do it?
Does it matter? I did it.

278
00:15:50,037 --> 00:15:52,582
Rigsby, we got a work address
on the suspect. Let's go.

279
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:54,751
- Uh, yeah.
- Uh, by the way, Grace

280
00:15:55,793 --> 00:15:58,254
there's a fabulous Thai place
on Sixth Street.

281
00:15:59,172 --> 00:16:01,549
They make a delicious Tom Kha Gai.

282
00:16:39,337 --> 00:16:40,379
Mr. Hutten?

283
00:16:45,426 --> 00:16:46,511
John Hutten?

284
00:16:49,514 --> 00:16:51,182
Put it down.
Let me see your hands.

285
00:16:52,433 --> 00:16:55,561
I'm Agent Lisbon with the CBI.
Just wanna ask you a few questions.

286
00:17:11,077 --> 00:17:12,453
Agent Lisbon, you said?

287
00:17:14,705 --> 00:17:15,748
Pleasure to meet you.

288
00:17:24,346 --> 00:17:26,264
John William Hutten.

289
00:17:26,723 --> 00:17:28,808
You were arrested twice
for grand theft auto.

290
00:17:28,933 --> 00:17:30,518
You served 18 months in Folsom.

291
00:17:31,269 --> 00:17:32,312
Here you are

292
00:17:32,479 --> 00:17:34,773
a suspect in a robbery
and homicide.

293
00:17:34,939 --> 00:17:36,983
Is there a charge
at the end of this, detective?

294
00:17:38,026 --> 00:17:39,444
Where were you yesterday
at noon?

295
00:17:41,029 --> 00:17:42,572
Home. Sick.

296
00:17:43,698 --> 00:17:45,200
Is there anyone
who can verify that?

297
00:17:46,868 --> 00:17:49,663
No, because I was home, sick.

298
00:17:51,081 --> 00:17:54,542
You were caught on camera
at four banks in the Central Valley.

299
00:17:55,085 --> 00:17:58,171
All four of those banks were robbed
within weeks of you visiting.

300
00:17:58,505 --> 00:18:00,298
Which is conclusive evidence
of what?

301
00:18:00,548 --> 00:18:02,550
I think it's evidence
that your client

302
00:18:02,676 --> 00:18:04,135
planned to commit armed robbery.

303
00:18:04,344 --> 00:18:06,638
Then charge him, and we'll see
what a jury has to say.

304
00:18:08,973 --> 00:18:10,517
What were you doing
in those banks?

305
00:18:12,727 --> 00:18:13,770
Times are tight.

306
00:18:13,895 --> 00:18:15,438
I was shopping
for competitive interest rates

307
00:18:15,563 --> 00:18:17,399
in money market accounts.

308
00:18:19,693 --> 00:18:21,152
And you've been smart so far.

309
00:18:21,569 --> 00:18:24,155
Blacking out security cameras,
going straight for the vault.

310
00:18:24,406 --> 00:18:26,950
But this time, you screwed up,
and somebody ended up dead.

311
00:18:27,367 --> 00:18:29,327
Maybe the SAC Fed job
was too big for you.

312
00:18:29,786 --> 00:18:32,455
O-or maybe the murder
was a part of the plan all along.

313
00:18:33,039 --> 00:18:35,375
I didn't rob Sacramento Federal.

314
00:18:35,917 --> 00:18:37,252
I didn't rob any bank.

315
00:18:38,294 --> 00:18:40,630
But if I did, I certainly wouldn't need
to kill someone.

316
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,507
That's just sloppy.

317
00:18:45,093 --> 00:18:47,721
Now I've had my brushes
with the law

318
00:18:48,263 --> 00:18:49,931
but I've learned some things
from them.

319
00:18:50,598 --> 00:18:54,310
Like the fact that you can't use
my past against me in court

320
00:18:55,145 --> 00:18:59,107
and no matter what you say
inside this little room

321
00:18:59,858 --> 00:19:01,317
you have nothing on me.

322
00:19:02,318 --> 00:19:04,779
So unless there's something else,
Agent Lisbon

323
00:19:05,405 --> 00:19:07,157
I think I should be getting
back to work.

324
00:19:08,450 --> 00:19:09,868
We'll see ourselves out.

325
00:19:17,709 --> 00:19:18,752
Hello.

326
00:19:19,169 --> 00:19:21,755
Patrick Jane. I'm working
the robbery-murder case.

327
00:19:22,046 --> 00:19:23,298
We already spoke with Agent Lisbon.

328
00:19:23,548 --> 00:19:25,258
Yes, I know.
I saw the whole thing.

329
00:19:25,425 --> 00:19:26,760
Uh, just a head's-up,
for future reference

330
00:19:26,885 --> 00:19:29,179
that large mirror is,
in fact, a window.

331
00:19:31,556 --> 00:19:33,892
- What do you want?
- Uh, I can see that you're a professional

332
00:19:34,017 --> 00:19:36,227
but, uh, Agent Lisbon was correct.
Uh...

333
00:19:36,478 --> 00:19:38,563
this last robbery
was a break in pattern.

334
00:19:38,772 --> 00:19:41,608
Uh, I don't mean that just
because someone was killed.

335
00:19:42,442 --> 00:19:44,194
I'm talking about the entire job.

336
00:19:44,778 --> 00:19:45,820
How's that?

337
00:19:46,154 --> 00:19:48,072
Well, the other three robberies
were simple--

338
00:19:48,198 --> 00:19:50,575
small town banks,
very little security

339
00:19:51,117 --> 00:19:52,160
straightforward.

340
00:19:52,577 --> 00:19:54,454
But SAC Federal--bigger.

341
00:19:55,079 --> 00:19:56,122
Much bigger.

342
00:19:56,247 --> 00:19:57,999
Mr. Jane, we've already answered.

343
00:19:58,166 --> 00:19:59,375
Now there had to be something

344
00:19:59,501 --> 00:20:01,544
that gave you
that extra bit of confidence

345
00:20:01,795 --> 00:20:02,837
to pull this one off.

346
00:20:03,630 --> 00:20:05,215
- What was that?
- John...

347
00:20:06,508 --> 00:20:07,550
Don't say a word.

348
00:20:09,385 --> 00:20:10,845
You had an inside man.

349
00:20:12,597 --> 00:20:13,640
Yes.

350
00:20:14,224 --> 00:20:15,266
Of course.

351
00:20:15,934 --> 00:20:19,103
I should've known. I used to use one
on occasion in my stage act.

352
00:20:22,774 --> 00:20:24,067
Stage act, huh?

353
00:20:24,692 --> 00:20:26,194
Uh, let me guess-- balloon sculpting?

354
00:20:26,736 --> 00:20:28,863
Animal impressions?
That's it.

355
00:20:32,242 --> 00:20:33,535
John's a good worker.

356
00:20:33,910 --> 00:20:36,246
Shows up on time,
keeps his mouth shut.

357
00:20:36,704 --> 00:20:38,081
Does he hang out
with any of his coworkers?

358
00:20:38,456 --> 00:20:40,416
Not that I've noticed.
Keeps to himself mostly.

359
00:20:40,708 --> 00:20:42,794
Has he been acting strange recently?

360
00:20:43,127 --> 00:20:44,170
Do anything out of the ordinary?

361
00:20:44,796 --> 00:20:46,047
Like come in in a dress?

362
00:20:48,716 --> 00:20:49,926
No. Nothing like that.

363
00:20:51,344 --> 00:20:53,555
Can you confirm whether or not Hutten
was at work on these dates?

364
00:20:56,015 --> 00:20:57,058
I can't help you.

365
00:20:57,517 --> 00:20:59,310
These are all before
John started working here.

366
00:20:59,978 --> 00:21:02,021
The last few days--
Hutten called in sick?

367
00:21:02,564 --> 00:21:04,899
Yeah, he said he had some
kind of bug. Couldn't get outta bed.

368
00:21:05,233 --> 00:21:06,276
You believe him?

369
00:21:06,484 --> 00:21:08,194
Sure. Why wouldn't I?
It's been going around.

370
00:21:08,611 --> 00:21:09,654
What do you mean by that?

371
00:21:10,029 --> 00:21:11,906
Two of my other guys
got the same thing.

372
00:21:12,407 --> 00:21:15,368
Arroyo brothers--
Jorge, Cesar.

373
00:21:17,579 --> 00:21:19,539
We're gonna need
their home address.

374
00:21:25,169 --> 00:21:26,462
{\an8}When are you getting
your shoes back?

375
00:21:28,131 --> 00:21:29,173
They're not so bad, are they?

376
00:21:48,651 --> 00:21:50,570
Are you sure this is
the right place to do this?

377
00:21:52,030 --> 00:21:54,866
Well, Hutten's inside man
works at the bank and it seems...

378
00:21:56,701 --> 00:21:59,495
Everyone that works at the bank
is here. I'll be right back.

379
00:21:59,913 --> 00:22:01,414
Jane, wait.
W--

380
00:22:03,833 --> 00:22:05,627
- Hello.
- Hello.

381
00:22:06,794 --> 00:22:08,963
Were you friends with my grandson?

382
00:22:11,591 --> 00:22:13,468
Perfect. Glad you're all here.

383
00:22:13,801 --> 00:22:14,969
Quick.
What's your favorite color?

384
00:22:15,094 --> 00:22:17,221
- What?
- Favorite color. Red? Green? Blue?

385
00:22:17,847 --> 00:22:18,890
Blue.

386
00:22:19,015 --> 00:22:20,892
Out of all your employees,
which is the least trustworthy?

387
00:22:21,267 --> 00:22:22,644
What? None of them.

388
00:22:23,353 --> 00:22:25,146
- You. What's your name?
- Casey.

389
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:27,106
Casey, you work in banking

390
00:22:27,315 --> 00:22:28,900
yet your personal finances
are a wreck.

391
00:22:29,067 --> 00:22:30,485
- No, they're not.
- Oh, please.

392
00:22:30,610 --> 00:22:32,612
That handbag on your salary?
Dead giveaway.

393
00:22:32,737 --> 00:22:34,781
And you bite your nails.
Sure sign of anxiety.

394
00:22:35,198 --> 00:22:37,575
Yet someone as anxious as you
probably doesn't have the stomach

395
00:22:37,867 --> 00:22:39,327
to pull off a crime like this.

396
00:22:39,911 --> 00:22:41,037
Crime? What crime?

397
00:22:42,664 --> 00:22:44,374
You didn't like Ernie, did you?

398
00:22:44,999 --> 00:22:46,334
You felt threatened by him.

399
00:22:47,126 --> 00:22:49,087
- Who told you that?
- You did just now.

400
00:22:49,379 --> 00:22:51,297
Clearly not smart enough
to pull off a robbery.

401
00:22:51,589 --> 00:22:52,966
- What'd you say to me?
- You heard me.

402
00:22:53,257 --> 00:22:56,511
Uh, when I asked your manager
who he trusted the least

403
00:22:57,387 --> 00:22:58,846
his eyes darted to you.

404
00:22:59,222 --> 00:23:00,765
- They did not.
- Repeat after me--

405
00:23:00,932 --> 00:23:04,060
- "I am the inside man."
- Hell, no.

406
00:23:04,310 --> 00:23:05,937
Just as I thought.
Not you either.

407
00:23:06,145 --> 00:23:08,481
Wait.
Th-there was an inside man?

408
00:23:09,148 --> 00:23:10,775
- What's your name?
- Uh, Tai.

409
00:23:10,942 --> 00:23:12,443
Tai. Pleasure to meet you.

410
00:23:13,111 --> 00:23:15,947
Have we met? Did you help rob
Sacramento Federal Bank?

411
00:23:16,114 --> 00:23:17,156
No!

412
00:23:17,281 --> 00:23:18,658
- You sure? Yes?
- Yeah. No!

413
00:23:18,783 --> 00:23:20,451
- No? Yes?
- Get off me.

414
00:23:20,576 --> 00:23:22,829
This--this is
completely inappropriate.

415
00:23:23,204 --> 00:23:24,914
Show Ernie some respect.

416
00:23:25,331 --> 00:23:26,374
Ernie.

417
00:23:28,251 --> 00:23:30,753
Yes. Ernie.
Absolutely right.

418
00:23:32,005 --> 00:23:33,047
My apologies.

419
00:23:44,225 --> 00:23:45,351
That was 1982?

420
00:23:46,728 --> 00:23:47,770
Yeah.

421
00:23:48,479 --> 00:23:50,273
Jane. Jane, where you going?

422
00:23:50,398 --> 00:23:52,108
I just have to check on something.
I'll be right back.

423
00:23:52,233 --> 00:23:53,693
- No.
- You know, you should probably answer that.

424
00:23:53,901 --> 00:23:55,778
- It's very important.
- Damn it, Jane.

425
00:23:56,863 --> 00:23:58,364
- Hello?
- "Hey, boss."

426
00:23:58,573 --> 00:24:00,283
We checked out
the Arroyo brothers' apartment.

427
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:01,743
Place is empty.

428
00:24:01,993 --> 00:24:04,162
According to the building manager
they took off late last night.

429
00:24:04,412 --> 00:24:05,580
Any word
on where they were going?

430
00:24:05,747 --> 00:24:07,290
No forwarding address
but they told the manager

431
00:24:07,415 --> 00:24:09,167
they were headed to Mexico
to visit family.

432
00:24:09,584 --> 00:24:11,586
And we also tracked down the van
that was used in the robbery.

433
00:24:11,836 --> 00:24:12,879
It was torched pretty bad.

434
00:24:14,589 --> 00:24:16,215
Yeah, it doesn't look like
we're gonna get anything form it.

435
00:24:16,924 --> 00:24:19,052
All right. Flag the Arroyo brothers
with customs.

436
00:24:19,302 --> 00:24:20,344
If they're on their way to Mexico

437
00:24:20,470 --> 00:24:21,971
maybe we can get them
before they cross the border.

438
00:24:22,263 --> 00:24:23,306
All right.

439
00:25:27,829 --> 00:25:28,871
Uh, Lisbon.

440
00:25:29,997 --> 00:25:31,040
Found something.

441
00:25:31,165 --> 00:25:33,543
You will never believe who was working
with the bank robbers.

442
00:25:35,503 --> 00:25:36,546
Ernie Wright.

443
00:25:40,633 --> 00:25:41,926
Probably shouldn't discuss it here.

444
00:25:48,015 --> 00:25:49,600
We're very sorry for your loss.

445
00:25:55,404 --> 00:25:56,738
There's no way Ernie could do
something like this.

446
00:25:56,905 --> 00:25:57,948
There's just no way.

447
00:25:58,449 --> 00:26:01,076
We found a one-way ticket
to Brazil in Ernie's name.

448
00:26:01,410 --> 00:26:02,453
No.

449
00:26:02,786 --> 00:26:04,830
No. That's absurd.

450
00:26:05,456 --> 00:26:06,498
Ernie?

451
00:26:07,082 --> 00:26:09,251
Robbing a bank?
I mean, he wasn't the type.

452
00:26:09,418 --> 00:26:10,711
He was exactly the type.

453
00:26:12,588 --> 00:26:15,466
Judging from these photographs here

454
00:26:15,716 --> 00:26:17,885
I'd say Ernie
became a different man.

455
00:26:18,302 --> 00:26:19,344
Yeah, he lost weight

456
00:26:19,636 --> 00:26:21,805
started dressing sharper.

457
00:26:22,389 --> 00:26:23,932
Powerful external transformations

458
00:26:24,057 --> 00:26:27,478
can often coincide
with even larger internal ones.

459
00:26:28,103 --> 00:26:29,354
He was trying to better himself.

460
00:26:29,771 --> 00:26:31,231
Why? Because of you?

461
00:26:31,857 --> 00:26:33,901
I encouraged him, of course.

462
00:26:34,193 --> 00:26:35,235
I loved him.

463
00:26:36,069 --> 00:26:37,946
Ernie was just a teller
when we met.

464
00:26:38,572 --> 00:26:39,698
He was still living at home.

465
00:26:40,741 --> 00:26:42,451
Shy, inexperienced with women?

466
00:26:43,118 --> 00:26:44,161
Yes.

467
00:26:44,495 --> 00:26:45,537
And what changed?

468
00:26:46,205 --> 00:26:47,331
He finished his degree

469
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:50,584
got promoted to assistant manager
and bought this house.

470
00:26:50,792 --> 00:26:52,878
And you were by his side
every step of the way.

471
00:26:53,128 --> 00:26:55,047
You must have seen something
very special in Ernie.

472
00:26:55,422 --> 00:26:56,465
Yes.

473
00:26:56,924 --> 00:26:58,550
I saw that he was sweet

474
00:26:59,218 --> 00:27:00,594
and how good a man he was.

475
00:27:02,179 --> 00:27:03,931
He could never do something
like this.

476
00:27:04,515 --> 00:27:05,557
No way.

477
00:27:08,477 --> 00:27:09,520
Where'd you grow up?

478
00:27:10,187 --> 00:27:11,230
Upstate New York.

479
00:27:11,855 --> 00:27:12,898
A town called Newburgh.

480
00:27:14,149 --> 00:27:15,192
And you two?

481
00:27:15,442 --> 00:27:16,485
Uh, Chicago.

482
00:27:18,820 --> 00:27:21,615
Here.
In Sacramento. Why?

483
00:27:22,157 --> 00:27:23,200
No reason.

484
00:27:24,993 --> 00:27:26,912
So if we prove Hutten's connection
to Ernie

485
00:27:27,037 --> 00:27:28,747
we prove Hutten's guilt.

486
00:27:29,206 --> 00:27:30,290
But a connection
should've come up by now.

487
00:27:30,415 --> 00:27:31,917
How did Hutten know Ernie?

488
00:27:32,376 --> 00:27:33,794
- Hot reading.
- What?

489
00:27:34,044 --> 00:27:36,296
Well, Hutten's a careful,
meticulous professional.

490
00:27:36,421 --> 00:27:38,924
He wouldn't have used an inside man
that could be traced back to him.

491
00:27:39,258 --> 00:27:41,093
So he researched
the staff at the bank.

492
00:27:41,301 --> 00:27:43,303
Hot reading.
Very easy to do these days.

493
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:46,515
And he kept digging until he found
someone with shaky ethics

494
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:47,766
and a yen for a better life--

495
00:27:48,433 --> 00:27:49,476
Ernie.

496
00:27:53,605 --> 00:27:54,648
Wow. It's late.

497
00:27:55,065 --> 00:27:56,275
What are you still doing here?

498
00:27:57,192 --> 00:27:59,653
Trying to find a connection
between Hutten and Ernie Wright.

499
00:28:00,529 --> 00:28:02,698
I've checked Ernie's e-mail account

500
00:28:03,031 --> 00:28:04,908
text messages,
and cell phone records.

501
00:28:05,117 --> 00:28:08,120
Nothing. So far there's no sign
of communication between them.

502
00:28:08,370 --> 00:28:09,454
Sorry to hear it.

503
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:12,040
Oh, listen, uh, the bank
manager's supposed to send out

504
00:28:12,165 --> 00:28:13,709
a list of safety deposit box owners.

505
00:28:13,875 --> 00:28:15,043
Right. It's on my desk.

506
00:28:15,419 --> 00:28:16,461
Thank you very much.

507
00:28:17,170 --> 00:28:18,589
Silly me. Almost forgot.

508
00:28:19,256 --> 00:28:21,174
I've really been craving
Italian lately

509
00:28:21,383 --> 00:28:24,469
so what do you say we get a nice linguine
for lunch tomorrow?

510
00:28:26,305 --> 00:28:27,514
- Okay?
- Yeah. Okay.

511
00:28:27,681 --> 00:28:28,724
Ciao. Ciao.

512
00:28:58,003 --> 00:28:59,046
Jane.

513
00:28:59,546 --> 00:29:01,131
- Jane, wake up.
- Yeah.

514
00:29:01,923 --> 00:29:03,133
- What's the time?
- 8:00.

515
00:29:03,508 --> 00:29:05,177
- Oh, we have to get going.
- Where?

516
00:29:05,594 --> 00:29:07,054
I'll explain it all in the car.

517
00:29:07,804 --> 00:29:09,640
No. You'll explain it now, please.

518
00:29:09,806 --> 00:29:12,059
Oh, I like it when you get
all authoritarian on me.

519
00:29:12,434 --> 00:29:15,103
- Talk. Where are we going?
- To catch Ernie's killer.

520
00:29:15,479 --> 00:29:16,897
How? We don't have anything
on Hutten.

521
00:29:17,105 --> 00:29:18,148
Hutten didn't kill Ernie.

522
00:29:18,649 --> 00:29:19,691
He didn't?

523
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:21,193
Well, he robbed the bank,
all right

524
00:29:21,318 --> 00:29:22,444
but he was telling the truth

525
00:29:22,611 --> 00:29:23,820
when he said he didn't need
to shoot anyone.

526
00:29:23,945 --> 00:29:26,615
Why would he do that?
It's sloppy, not his style.

527
00:29:26,948 --> 00:29:28,909
Jane, I need more than that.

528
00:29:30,035 --> 00:29:32,704
You remember the safe deposit vault
was open during the robbery?

529
00:29:33,497 --> 00:29:36,166
I just assumed that someone took
something from there

530
00:29:36,291 --> 00:29:37,459
but, uh, I got it all backwards.

531
00:29:37,626 --> 00:29:39,419
They didn't take anything.

532
00:29:39,961 --> 00:29:41,505
They put something in there.

533
00:29:42,089 --> 00:29:43,131
What?

534
00:29:43,507 --> 00:29:45,842
You really want me to tell you?
It's gonna ruin the surprise.

535
00:29:46,093 --> 00:29:48,720
- Yes. I don't like surprises.
- Three guesses then.

536
00:29:50,764 --> 00:29:51,807
I'll give you a hint.

537
00:29:53,016 --> 00:29:55,227
It's--it's not animal

538
00:29:55,519 --> 00:29:56,561
or vegetable.

539
00:30:04,152 --> 00:30:07,197
You know, we can't open a safe deposit
box without a warrant.

540
00:30:07,739 --> 00:30:09,491
We can if we have
the owner's permission.

541
00:30:13,537 --> 00:30:15,497
Uh, we don't open
for a half-hour.

542
00:30:15,831 --> 00:30:17,040
Is everything all right?

543
00:30:17,457 --> 00:30:18,500
Everything's fine.

544
00:30:18,625 --> 00:30:20,293
We just want to ask your employees
some questions.

545
00:30:20,419 --> 00:30:21,461
It shouldn't take long.

546
00:30:21,628 --> 00:30:24,131
Can you have everyone who was here
at the time of the robbery

547
00:30:24,256 --> 00:30:26,925
gather in the safe deposit vault,
yourself included?

548
00:30:27,134 --> 00:30:29,720
Yes, absolutely.
Has there been a break in the case?

549
00:30:29,845 --> 00:30:30,887
You'll see.

550
00:30:39,104 --> 00:30:40,188
What's this all about?

551
00:30:40,564 --> 00:30:42,983
Oh, I've gathered you here
to help catch Ernie's killer.

552
00:30:43,400 --> 00:30:45,193
How are we gonna catch
the bank robber?

553
00:30:45,318 --> 00:30:47,195
Well, the bank robber
didn't kill Ernie.

554
00:30:47,696 --> 00:30:49,489
- Then who did?
- Uh, one of you.

555
00:30:50,490 --> 00:30:52,409
- What?
- I don't think so, buddy.

556
00:30:52,701 --> 00:30:55,787
- I would never hurt Ernie.
- Whoa. There's no need for objections.

557
00:30:56,204 --> 00:30:58,165
One of you shot Ernie
during the robbery

558
00:30:58,290 --> 00:31:00,125
and you hid the gun
in a safe deposit box.

559
00:31:00,375 --> 00:31:02,252
- I am sure of it.
- But that--

560
00:31:02,461 --> 00:31:03,503
Yes, exactly, Doug.

561
00:31:03,670 --> 00:31:05,464
That means the killer would've had
to have planned the murder

562
00:31:05,756 --> 00:31:06,923
a long way in advance

563
00:31:07,048 --> 00:31:09,426
so one of you,
who I will identify shortly

564
00:31:10,218 --> 00:31:11,887
is a cold-blooded schemer.

565
00:31:13,138 --> 00:31:14,181
Now first of all

566
00:31:14,306 --> 00:31:17,434
if there's anyone here
that feels the urge to leave feel free.

567
00:31:17,559 --> 00:31:19,060
Please do so. But know this--

568
00:31:19,644 --> 00:31:21,313
we will assume you are our killer.

569
00:31:22,314 --> 00:31:25,442
Armin, if you wouldn't mind
unlocking the vault door.

570
00:31:27,652 --> 00:31:28,695
Thank you.

571
00:31:41,906 --> 00:31:42,949
Before we begin

572
00:31:43,324 --> 00:31:47,412
uh, Agent Lisbon has a few words.
Agent Lisbon?

573
00:31:47,787 --> 00:31:50,039
I've been authorized
by the district attorney's office

574
00:31:50,164 --> 00:31:52,500
to offer Ernie's killer a plea deal.

575
00:31:53,251 --> 00:31:54,669
Ten years in prison

576
00:31:54,836 --> 00:31:57,547
if you cooperate now
and open the deposit box.

577
00:31:58,256 --> 00:31:59,298
Ten years.

578
00:32:00,591 --> 00:32:01,801
That's a very generous offer.

579
00:32:02,343 --> 00:32:03,553
And all you have to do

580
00:32:04,262 --> 00:32:06,723
is open the box
before I'm forced to.

581
00:32:11,436 --> 00:32:12,478
Just as I'd hoped.

582
00:32:26,534 --> 00:32:27,577
Here.

583
00:32:29,662 --> 00:32:31,372
Definitely somewhere here.

584
00:32:32,749 --> 00:32:33,791
You sure?

585
00:32:34,042 --> 00:32:35,084
Positive.

586
00:32:37,879 --> 00:32:39,547
The offer is now 15 years.

587
00:32:39,797 --> 00:32:41,049
All right, this is absurd.

588
00:32:41,340 --> 00:32:43,593
You can't play some game
with people's lives.

589
00:32:43,718 --> 00:32:46,137
Armin, we're the law.
We can do whatever we want.

590
00:32:46,262 --> 00:32:47,764
Any takers for 15 years?

591
00:32:49,974 --> 00:32:51,017
Very well.

592
00:32:52,518 --> 00:32:57,106
Mm, not really feeling it.

593
00:33:00,693 --> 00:33:04,322
Yes.
It's somewhere in this group here.

594
00:33:06,407 --> 00:33:08,159
The offer is now 20 years.

595
00:33:08,367 --> 00:33:10,536
20 years right now.
There it is.

596
00:33:10,661 --> 00:33:13,206
Your last chance of seeing freedom
in your lifetime.

597
00:33:13,831 --> 00:33:16,250
All you need is a little key
that fits in a little lock.

598
00:33:19,545 --> 00:33:20,588
Suit yourselves.

599
00:33:22,048 --> 00:33:23,091
I believe...

600
00:33:25,218 --> 00:33:27,595
It's one of these three here.

601
00:33:30,973 --> 00:33:32,892
Starting on five.
Starting on five.

602
00:33:33,142 --> 00:33:34,227
Uh, Stephens

603
00:33:35,895 --> 00:33:37,897
Hudson, Keene.

604
00:33:40,399 --> 00:33:43,444
- Stephens, Hudson, Keene.
- 25 years.

605
00:33:44,028 --> 00:33:46,322
If we have to force open
the box, the deal's off.

606
00:33:47,323 --> 00:33:48,950
You'll be facing
first-degree murder

607
00:33:49,075 --> 00:33:50,118
and the district attorney

608
00:33:50,243 --> 00:33:51,953
will aggressively pursue
the death penalty.

609
00:33:52,245 --> 00:33:53,579
You might get life if you're lucky.

610
00:33:56,749 --> 00:33:59,710
- All right, Jane. Which one is it?
- Yeah. Yeah. Uh, Stephens...

611
00:34:01,003 --> 00:34:02,421
No. No.

612
00:34:06,759 --> 00:34:07,802
Keene?

613
00:34:08,344 --> 00:34:09,595
No, I don't think so.

614
00:34:12,056 --> 00:34:14,016
- Perhaps it's Hudson.
- Wait.

615
00:34:21,482 --> 00:34:22,525
Nancy?

616
00:34:22,984 --> 00:34:26,404
- I knew it.
- Oh, my God. You evil bitch!

617
00:34:26,946 --> 00:34:28,906
There's no need for that.
Let's see if the key fits.

618
00:34:29,115 --> 00:34:30,158
Shall we?

619
00:34:48,426 --> 00:34:51,179
Nancy Sterling, you're under arrest
for the murder of Ernie Wright.

620
00:34:51,554 --> 00:34:53,306
Turn around. Put your hands
behind your back.

621
00:34:57,476 --> 00:34:59,353
When I met Ernie, he was a loser.

622
00:35:00,104 --> 00:35:03,482
Fat, stuck in his job,
still living with his parents.

623
00:35:05,860 --> 00:35:06,903
And you helped him change?

624
00:35:07,403 --> 00:35:08,446
Helped him?

625
00:35:08,946 --> 00:35:10,698
I made him the man he was.

626
00:35:11,490 --> 00:35:13,367
I supported him
when he went back to school

627
00:35:13,784 --> 00:35:14,827
found him his house

628
00:35:15,286 --> 00:35:16,662
I even helped him get promoted.

629
00:35:17,413 --> 00:35:18,915
And how did he repay me?

630
00:35:19,498 --> 00:35:21,417
He completely lost interest
in me.

631
00:35:22,335 --> 00:35:23,502
And you resented him for it.

632
00:35:23,961 --> 00:35:25,004
You're damn right I did.

633
00:35:27,465 --> 00:35:28,507
I thought he was cheating on me.

634
00:35:29,842 --> 00:35:30,968
He was getting in shape

635
00:35:31,844 --> 00:35:32,887
working out.

636
00:35:33,846 --> 00:35:35,973
Don't think I didn't notice
other women looking at him.

637
00:35:37,391 --> 00:35:38,684
"You should've seen Ernie."

638
00:35:39,810 --> 00:35:40,853
"He loved it."

639
00:35:42,230 --> 00:35:43,689
Is that when you began
spying on him?

640
00:35:44,565 --> 00:35:47,151
I checked his phone, his e-mail.

641
00:35:48,236 --> 00:35:51,113
One time I followed him
into one of those Internet cafes.

642
00:35:51,906 --> 00:35:52,949
So shady.

643
00:35:54,492 --> 00:35:56,077
He was using a secret e-mail account.

644
00:35:56,202 --> 00:35:57,453
Which you hacked into.

645
00:35:58,079 --> 00:35:59,455
That's when I found the e-mails.

646
00:35:59,705 --> 00:36:02,291
And you're referring to the correspondence
between Ernie and John Hutten, right?

647
00:36:02,708 --> 00:36:04,710
More like step-by-step details

648
00:36:04,919 --> 00:36:06,754
outlining how they were gonna rob
the bank.

649
00:36:09,257 --> 00:36:10,341
I didn't know what to do.

650
00:36:12,385 --> 00:36:14,553
But then I found
that ticket to Brazil.

651
00:36:16,389 --> 00:36:17,807
Ernie was gonna leave me.

652
00:36:18,891 --> 00:36:21,811
Me, after everything
I'd done for him.

653
00:36:23,396 --> 00:36:24,438
I don't think so.

654
00:36:26,941 --> 00:36:28,734
"I had the details for the robbery."

655
00:36:29,819 --> 00:36:32,863
"I knew exactly where everyone
was going to be"

656
00:36:33,239 --> 00:36:34,907
"and when they were
going to be there."

657
00:36:38,202 --> 00:36:39,245
"So I hid."

658
00:36:40,288 --> 00:36:41,872
"And I waited
for the robbers to leave."

659
00:36:46,419 --> 00:36:47,670
"Then went into the cash vault."

660
00:36:50,423 --> 00:36:52,174
"Ernie never suspected
a thing."

661
00:36:53,926 --> 00:36:56,178
- "I'm keeping the ring."
- "What are you--"

662
00:37:02,935 --> 00:37:04,603
"You should've seen the look
on his face."

663
00:37:06,355 --> 00:37:07,398
"It was perfect."

664
00:37:08,649 --> 00:37:10,192
"Except for one thing."

665
00:37:14,905 --> 00:37:17,241
"I left the safe deposit vault door open."

666
00:37:22,705 --> 00:37:24,373
"When I tried to go back
and close it"

667
00:37:26,167 --> 00:37:27,209
"it was too late."

668
00:37:33,007 --> 00:37:34,508
You know, you could've
just called the police.

669
00:37:36,052 --> 00:37:38,471
- Turned Ernie in.
- I thought about that.

670
00:37:39,221 --> 00:37:40,264
I really did.

671
00:37:41,390 --> 00:37:43,476
But Ernie was gonna leave me.

672
00:37:44,393 --> 00:37:45,436
Me.

673
00:37:46,520 --> 00:37:48,064
I was planning our wedding

674
00:37:48,439 --> 00:37:50,858
and he was just
gonna disappear forever.

675
00:37:54,070 --> 00:37:56,322
He deserved everything he got.

676
00:38:03,871 --> 00:38:06,374
This is getting to be grounds
for harassment, Agent Lisbon.

677
00:38:06,499 --> 00:38:08,250
I told him this wouldn't take long.

678
00:38:08,834 --> 00:38:11,796
"I will arrive Tuesday
at 12:00 p.m. exactly."

679
00:38:11,962 --> 00:38:13,005
"You will be in the lobby."

680
00:38:13,214 --> 00:38:15,466
"I will take you in
back at gunpoint"

681
00:38:15,591 --> 00:38:16,675
"where you will open the vault."

682
00:38:18,052 --> 00:38:20,679
"You will help load the cash
into duffel bags"

683
00:38:20,805 --> 00:38:22,515
"then you will stay behind."

684
00:38:25,518 --> 00:38:27,728
Ernie's fiancée was spying on him.

685
00:38:27,978 --> 00:38:29,230
Text messages, phone calls.

686
00:38:29,355 --> 00:38:31,399
She even found the secret e-mail account
that he was using.

687
00:38:31,690 --> 00:38:34,985
As a matter of fact, she saved
every e-mail you sent him.

688
00:38:36,195 --> 00:38:37,613
You ready to talk
about that deal now?

689
00:38:40,491 --> 00:38:43,577
Hutten wasn't the killer so it had
to be somebody else in the bank

690
00:38:43,869 --> 00:38:45,162
but why Nancy?

691
00:38:46,247 --> 00:38:48,791
Whoever killed Ernie had to have known
about the robbery in advance.

692
00:38:48,916 --> 00:38:51,460
Well, Nancy was, uh,
the likely candidate.

693
00:38:51,919 --> 00:38:54,630
- She's also a classic power dater.
- A what?

694
00:38:54,839 --> 00:38:56,173
Oh, you know the type.

695
00:38:58,300 --> 00:39:01,887
They date down so they have
all the power in a relationship.

696
00:39:02,054 --> 00:39:04,557
Oh.
And how did you know this?

697
00:39:06,559 --> 00:39:11,355
Uh, well, she had more than half
of the space in Ernie's closet.

698
00:39:11,480 --> 00:39:12,857
I mean, she didn't even live there

699
00:39:12,982 --> 00:39:15,151
and she had more than half
of his closet space?

700
00:39:16,110 --> 00:39:18,737
And how did you know which
safe deposit box was Nancy's?

701
00:39:18,946 --> 00:39:19,989
I hot read her.

702
00:39:20,322 --> 00:39:22,825
I had the list of owners
and the bank staff files.

703
00:39:23,075 --> 00:39:25,244
I knew one of the names
had to be Nancy in disguise.

704
00:39:25,619 --> 00:39:26,662
Hudson?

705
00:39:28,539 --> 00:39:31,500
No one ever strays very far
when it comes to false names.

706
00:39:32,209 --> 00:39:34,920
Nancy said that she grew up in
a small town in upstate New York--

707
00:39:35,254 --> 00:39:37,423
- Newburgh.
- On the Hudson River.

708
00:39:37,631 --> 00:39:39,008
On the Hudson River.

709
00:39:39,341 --> 00:39:41,177
You know, these shoes are actually
quite comfortable.

710
00:39:42,136 --> 00:39:43,387
They're growing on me.

711
00:39:46,223 --> 00:39:47,683
- Not on me.
- No?

712
00:39:58,861 --> 00:40:00,779
Oh, hey, Teresa.
Glad you made it.

713
00:40:01,906 --> 00:40:04,492
It's a pretty high-class crowd.
I wish you would've warned me.

714
00:40:04,825 --> 00:40:06,827
Nah. They're pussycats.
Come on. I'll introduce you.

715
00:40:08,204 --> 00:40:09,955
Teresa Lisbon, this is district attorney

716
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:11,165
- Don Wolcott.
- Hi.

717
00:40:11,290 --> 00:40:13,584
- FBI Bureau Director, Charles Bailey...
- Sir.

718
00:40:13,834 --> 00:40:16,045
- Senator Eileen Dawkins.
- State Senator.

719
00:40:16,504 --> 00:40:18,464
Here. Have a seat.
Get you a drink?

720
00:40:18,589 --> 00:40:20,257
Yeah. Can I have a scotch
on the rocks, please?

721
00:40:20,424 --> 00:40:21,467
You got it.

722
00:40:22,218 --> 00:40:24,553
- Oh, I think you know this guy, right?
- Teresa.

723
00:40:26,597 --> 00:40:28,057
I didn't take you for a gambler.

724
00:40:28,766 --> 00:40:30,643
Oh, it's not gambling
if you know you're gonna win.

725
00:40:33,979 --> 00:40:35,397
Well, we got a live one.
Watch out.

726
00:40:42,780 --> 00:40:44,740
Look at that, huh?
Beautiful work.

727
00:40:44,949 --> 00:40:45,991
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

728
00:40:51,121 --> 00:40:52,164
Okay. Here.

729
00:40:55,334 --> 00:40:56,377
There we go.

730
00:41:03,133 --> 00:41:04,176
For the rental.

731
00:41:07,513 --> 00:41:09,640
Thank you. Good night, Mr. Jane.

732
00:41:09,807 --> 00:41:11,267
- Good night.
- Good night, Niko.

733
00:41:14,353 --> 00:41:15,688
I'm headed home.
I'll see you tomorrow.

734
00:41:15,980 --> 00:41:18,774
Uh, yeah, tomorrow--
curry, definitely.

735
00:41:19,358 --> 00:41:20,401
I feel like some Indian.

736
00:41:21,443 --> 00:41:23,571
You gotta tell me. How did
you come up with Hutten's name?

737
00:41:23,946 --> 00:41:24,989
It's driving me crazy.

738
00:41:27,157 --> 00:41:28,200
Fair enough.

739
00:41:29,159 --> 00:41:31,704
Get a pen and some paper.
Write down a name, any name.

740
00:41:44,258 --> 00:41:45,301
Wayne Rigsby.

741
00:41:47,428 --> 00:41:48,470
You guessed?

742
00:41:48,679 --> 00:41:50,973
No. Although with that name,
it wouldn't be hard to.

743
00:41:51,348 --> 00:41:53,017
I, uh, read your pen.

744
00:41:53,892 --> 00:41:56,228
- So you cheated?
- That's a dirty word.

745
00:41:57,187 --> 00:41:58,230
Maybe just a little.

746
00:42:03,027 --> 00:42:04,153
Well, here's what I think
of your little trick.

747
00:42:07,573 --> 00:42:08,991
I didn't quite get the first word

748
00:42:09,116 --> 00:42:10,784
but the second word was
definitely "you".

749
00:42:12,286 --> 00:42:13,329
Good night.

750
00:42:23,547 --> 00:42:25,257
Oh, well, that's not very nice.

